-- InstanceDropSources.lua
-- Xal's Armoire - which dungeon/raid and boss drops each item, across every
-- expansion in the game's history.
--
-- GENERATED by merging every instance_*.lua research file in
-- D:\WoW_Addons\Dev\armoire_research\ (see merge_instances.py). Do not
-- hand-edit this file; edit the research files and regenerate.
--
-- 12827 unique itemIDs across 224 dungeons/raids,
-- 1385 unique (instance, boss) pairs.
--
-- Three-level share, same technique AllTheThings uses for its own database
-- (confirmed by reading its real installed files, MIT-licensed): a named-key
-- table per entry ({instance=,kind=,boss=}) would mean ~12,500 separate hash
-- tables. Instead:
--   InstanceList[i]         = {name, kind}         - one entry per instance
--   InstanceBossPairs[p]     = {instanceIndex, boss} - one entry per (instance,
--                              boss) combination, shared by every item that
--                              boss drops (a dungeon's ~25 items collapse to
--                              the ~4 pairs its bosses actually need)
--   InstanceDropSources[id]  = pairIndex           - a plain NUMBER per item,
--                              not a table at all

